  "notes": "West leads the ♠Q against 6♠. West's trump lead is won by South. South should cash another high trump which reveals the 3-1 break. West must have the ♣A to go with his trump trick for his double. West has at most 1 diamond given East's 5 level preempt.\n\nSouth's basic plan should be to ruff North's clubs in the South hand. If South can score all 5 of his small trumps in this way the contract will be home. To accomplish this, dummy will need 4 heart entries along with the ♦A.\n\nSouth starts by leading the ♥K to the ♥A and a club is ruffed. South plays a heart and when West follows low, the ♥10 or ♥9 is played from dummy. If East discards, South will have no trouble scoring all 4 of his small trumps by ruffing clubs as West follows.\n\nIf East follows with a small heart, another club is ruffed. South crosses to the ♦A, cashes the ♥Q, and plays a third club, ruffing in hand. South exits a trump to West. West is down to all clubs. He will exit with the ♣A, ruffed by South. North has an entry in hearts to reach the ♣K.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
